course: dictionary
lesson: 13339
title: Habitual: what you always do
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A habit is something you do so often that it almost happens by itself. Habitual is the adjective for that. It describes something done often, as a habit. «Ravi takes his habitual walk after dinner» means the walk he always takes, again and again.
explain: Context gives you the clues. «Mia is a habitual latecomer» tells you she is late again and again, not just once. Try your meaning in place of the hard word: «Mia is a usual latecomer» still makes sense, so habitual means usual, done over and over.
explain: Habitual can describe good things or bad things. «Her habitual swim keeps her fit» is good, but «habitual lying» is not. The word itself does not say which, so the words around it tell you. Habit is the noun, and habitual is the adjective.
fact: Habitual is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a habitual walk, a habitual liar.
fact: «Habitual» means done often, as a habit.
fact: «Habitual» can also mean usual, as in «her habitual seat».
fact: «Habitual» often describes doing something bad again and again, as in «a habitual liar».
fact: Habit is the noun, and habitual is the adjective that goes with it.
exercise: «Every morning Sam takes his habitual walk to the shop.» What does habitual mean here? | Very fast | *Done as a usual habit, again and again | Done only once, by accident | Forgotten
exercise: «Jo is a habitual latecomer.» What does habitual suggest? | She is lost | *She is late again and again | She never comes at all | She is early every day
exercise: What is the noun that goes with habitual? | *Habit | Hobby | Hermit | Habitat
test: «The dog's habitual place is by the fire.» What does habitual mean? | Cold | Far away | *Usual | Broken
test: Which sentence uses habitual to describe something good? | *«Her habitual swim keeps her fit.» | «They are habitual thieves.» | «She is a habitual cheat.» | «He is a habitual liar.»
exam: Which word means the same as habitual in «her habitual seat»? | Empty | *Usual | Hasty | Seat
